IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `ei4-part-vi-review`
IMPORT `ei4-part-vi-investigation-and-proof`
IMPORT `ei4-part-vi-certificates-and-inspections`
IMPORT `ei4-part-vi-proceedings-and-evidence`
IMPORT `ei4-part-vi-offences-and-sin`
IMPORT `ei4-part-vii-benefit-repayment`
IMPORT `ei4-parts-viii-viii3`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Parts VI, VII, VIII, VIII.1, VIII.2 and VIII.3 -- THE SEAT LAYER (piece ei4).
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has lost work, or cannot work because of sickness, pregnancy, caring for a child or a family member, or who is
-- self-employed or a fisher, asking whether they qualify for Employment Insurance benefits, how many hours or weeks they need, how much
-- they would receive and for how long, and what they must do or tell the Commission. In Parts VI to VIII.3 that person asks: can a
-- decision about my claim be changed or appealed, and am I paid meanwhile; what may the Commission and its agents do to me (prosecute,
-- certify a debt, garnish my pay, inspect, demand information); what must I do and what can I be fined for; must I repay benefits
-- because my income was high, how much, and by when; and do the special rules of the alternate-access scheme and the interim orders reach me.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, numbers, dates -- one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc
-- worded as the person would be asked. The records the layer-1 modules expect (a request for reconsideration, an affidavit, the conduct
-- alleged under s 135(1), the benefits paid in a year) are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME
-- layer-1 rule is then called; no rule is restated here. A record field that the rule called never reads is given a fixed placeholder,
-- with a comment saying so. A MAYBE input of a layer-1 rule is asked as a yes/no and a date, and the date is ignored on "no".
-- A judgment the Act leaves to the Commission, a judge or the Minister of National Revenue is asked as a conditional ("if the Commission
-- is satisfied that ..."), never guessed. The maximum yearly insurable earnings is the published figure for the year (not in the text).
-- FALSE from a question that asks whether a power or an effect applies means "this provision does not give it", not "it is forbidden".
-- Not asked from this seat (no question, with the reason in NOTES.md): the powers and duties of a judge, of the Governor in Council and of
-- the Commission among themselves; the third-party and employer sides of garnishment and service (ss 126(5)(b), (7), (8), (9), (16) to (19)),
-- which belong to an employer seat that is not written here; and the court mechanics of authenticity (ss 125(1), (9) to (13), (16),
-- 126(20), 134(1), (3), (4)).
-- The employer's, the third party's and the Crown's side of each relation is in layer 1, under the same rule.

§ `Employment Insurance Act Parts VI to VIII.3 -- the questions of a person who claims or has claimed benefits`

§§ `Review of a decision about my claim (ss 111 to 114)`

-- SITUATION: the Commission has made a decision about your claim, or a tribunal has decided an appeal. Ask "Has the Commission made a
-- decision about your claim?" before showing this group.
-- s 111. "Rescind or amend": cancel or change a decision already given. The Commission may do so on new facts, or when it is satisfied
-- that the decision was given without knowledge of, or was based on a mistake as to, some material fact.
@export Can the Commission rescind or amend its decision on my claim (s 111)?
GIVEN `new facts have been presented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have new facts been presented to the Commission about your claim?
      `the Commission is satisfied that the decision was given without knowledge of a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commission satisfied that its decision was given without knowledge of some material fact?
      `the Commission is satisfied that the decision was based on a mistake as to a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commission satisfied that its decision was based on a mistake as to some material fact?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission rescind or amend its decision on my claim` IF
    `s 111 the Commission may rescind or amend a decision given in a claim for benefits` `new facts have been presented` `the Commission is satisfied that the decision was given without knowledge of a material fact` `the Commission is satisfied that the decision was based on a mistake as to a material fact`

-- ss 112(1) and 112.1. "Reconsideration": asking the Commission to look at its own decision again. The claimant, anyone else the decision
-- is about, or the claimant's employer may ask, in the prescribed form and manner, within 30 days after the decision was communicated
-- or any further time the Commission allows. A decision about writing off a penalty, an amount owing or interest cannot be reconsidered.
@export May I ask the Commission to reconsider its decision, and is my request in time (ss 112(1), 112.1)?
GIVEN `I am the claimant or another person the decision is about` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the claimant, or another person who is the subject of the Commission's decision?
      `I am the employer of the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the employer of the claimant?
      `my request is in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request in the form and manner the Regulations prescribe (in writing, with the information regulation 78 lists, filed as the Commission directs)?
      `the day the decision was communicated to me` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the decision communicated to you? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the day I make my request` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make, or did you make, your request? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the Commission has allowed me further time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission allowed you more than the 30 days to make your request?
      `the last day of the further time` IS A DATE @desc If the Commission allowed you further time, the last day it allowed (YYYY-MM-DD). If not, give any date: it is ignored.
      `the decision was made under the Employment Insurance Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision made under the Employment Insurance Regulations?
      `the decision is about writing off a penalty, an amount owing, or interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision about writing off a penalty you owe, an amount you owe, or interest on either?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the Commission to reconsider its decision and is my request in time` IF
    `s 112(1) a request for reconsideration is made under subsection (1)` `my request` `the decision cannot be reviewed`
    WHERE
        `my request` MEANS `ei4 Request for reconsideration` WITH
            `the requester is a claimant or other person who is the subject of the decision` IS `I am the claimant or another person the decision is about`
            `the requester is the employer of the claimant` IS `I am the employer of the claimant`
            `the request is in the prescribed form and manner` IS `my request is in the prescribed form and manner`
            `the day on which the decision is communicated to the requester` IS `the day the decision was communicated to me`
            `the day on which the request is made` IS `the day I make my request`
            `the last day of any further time the Commission has allowed` IS IF `the Commission has allowed me further time` THEN JUST `the last day of the further time` ELSE NOTHING
        -- Only whether any one of the three write-off topics applies is read by s 112.1, so one answer feeds the first and the others are fixed.
        `the decision cannot be reviewed` MEANS `s 112.1 the decision is not subject to review under section 112` `the decision was made under the Employment Insurance Regulations` `the decision is about writing off a penalty, an amount owing, or interest` FALSE FALSE

-- s 112(2). The Commission's duty is the other side of the same request: it "must reconsider its decision if a request is made".
@export Must the Commission reconsider its decision if I ask (s 112(2))?
GIVEN `I am the claimant or another person the decision is about` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the claimant, or another person who is the subject of the Commission's decision?
      `I am the employer of the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the employer of the claimant?
      `my request is in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request in the form and manner the Regulations prescribe (in writing, with the information regulation 78 lists, filed as the Commission directs)?
      `the day the decision was communicated to me` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the decision communicated to you? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the day I make my request` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make, or did you make, your request? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the Commission has allowed me further time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission allowed you more than the 30 days to make your request?
      `the last day of the further time` IS A DATE @desc If the Commission allowed you further time, the last day it allowed (YYYY-MM-DD). If not, give any date: it is ignored.
      `the decision was made under the Employment Insurance Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision made under the Employment Insurance Regulations?
      `the decision is about writing off a penalty, an amount owing, or interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision about writing off a penalty you owe, an amount you owe, or interest on either?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commission reconsider its decision if I ask` IF
    `s 112(2) the Commission must reconsider its decision` `my request` `the decision cannot be reviewed`
    WHERE
        `my request` MEANS `ei4 Request for reconsideration` WITH
            `the requester is a claimant or other person who is the subject of the decision` IS `I am the claimant or another person the decision is about`
            `the requester is the employer of the claimant` IS `I am the employer of the claimant`
            `the request is in the prescribed form and manner` IS `my request is in the prescribed form and manner`
            `the day on which the decision is communicated to the requester` IS `the day the decision was communicated to me`
            `the day on which the request is made` IS `the day I make my request`
            `the last day of any further time the Commission has allowed` IS IF `the Commission has allowed me further time` THEN JUST `the last day of the further time` ELSE NOTHING
        -- Only whether any one of the three write-off topics applies is read by s 112.1, so one answer feeds the first and the others are fixed.
        `the decision cannot be reviewed` MEANS `s 112.1 the decision is not subject to review under section 112` `the decision was made under the Employment Insurance Regulations` `the decision is about writing off a penalty, an amount owing, or interest` FALSE FALSE

-- s 112(1)(a). The thirty days run from the day after the decision is communicated and the thirtieth day counts.
@export What is the last day I can ask the Commission to reconsider without needing more time (s 112(1)(a))?
GIVEN `the day the decision was communicated to me` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the decision communicated to you? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day I can ask for a reconsideration without more time` IS
    `s 112(1)(a) the last day to request a reconsideration within 30 days` `the day the decision was communicated to me`

-- s 113. "Appeal": asking the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal to decide again. The time limit is in the Department of Employment and
-- Social Development Act, which this encoding does not hold, so no deadline is given.
@export Can I appeal to the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal (s 113)?
GIVEN `I am a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the decision?
      `I am dissatisfied with the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you dissatisfied with the decision?
      `the decision was made under section 112` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision made on a request for reconsideration under section 112?
      `the decision is about further time to make a request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision about whether you could have further time to ask for a reconsideration?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I appeal to the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal` IF
    `s 113 a party may appeal the decision to the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal` `I am a party` `I am dissatisfied with the decision` `the decision was made under section 112` `the decision is about further time to make a request`

-- s 114(1) with (2). If a tribunal or the Board of Appeal allowed your claim, you are paid in line with that decision even while the
-- Commission appeals, unless the Commission appealed within 21 days on the ground that you ought to be disentitled under section 36, or
-- your case is one the Regulations prescribe.
@export Am I paid benefits while an appeal of the decision that allowed my claim is pending (s 114)?
GIVEN `my claim was allowed by the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your claim allowed by the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal?
      `my claim was allowed by the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your claim allowed by the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal?
      `the day the decision allowing my claim was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the decision that allowed your claim given? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the day the Commission's appeal to the Appeal Division was brought` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Commission bring its appeal to the Appeal Division? (YYYY-MM-DD; if there is no such appeal, give any date)
      `the Commission appealed on the ground that I ought to be disentitled under section 36` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission appeal on the ground that you ought to be disentitled under section 36?
      `my case is one the Regulations prescribe as an exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your case one the Commission has prescribed by regulation as an exception (regulations 80 to 82)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I paid benefits while an appeal of the decision allowing my claim is pending` IF
    `s 114(1) benefits are payable in accordance with the decision even though an appeal is pending` `my claim was allowed by the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal` `my claim was allowed by the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal` `the exception applies`
    WHERE
        `the exception applies` MEANS `s 114(2) subsection (1) does not apply` `the day the decision allowing my claim was given` `the day the Commission's appeal to the Appeal Division was brought` `the Commission appealed on the ground that I ought to be disentitled under section 36` `my case is one the Regulations prescribe as an exception`

-- s 114(1), second limb. Benefits paid to you after the decision are treated as duly paid and cannot be recovered from you, even if the
-- final answer goes against you. TRUE means s 114(1) protects you; FALSE means s 114(1) gives you no such protection (it does not say
-- the benefits can be recovered).
@export Are the benefits paid to me after that decision protected from recovery even if the appeal goes against me (s 114(1))?
GIVEN `my claim was allowed by the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your claim allowed by the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal?
      `my claim was allowed by the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your claim allowed by the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal?
      `the day the decision allowing my claim was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the decision that allowed your claim given? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the day the Commission's appeal to the Appeal Division was brought` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Commission bring its appeal to the Appeal Division? (YYYY-MM-DD; if there is no such appeal, give any date)
      `the Commission appealed on the ground that I ought to be disentitled under section 36` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission appeal on the ground that you ought to be disentitled under section 36?
      `my case is one the Regulations prescribe as an exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your case one the Commission has prescribed by regulation as an exception (regulations 80 to 82)?
      `the benefits were paid to me after the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the benefits paid to you after the decision that allowed your claim?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the benefits paid to me after the decision protected from recovery` IF
    `s 114(1) benefits paid after the decision are treated as duly paid and are not recoverable from the claimant` `my claim was allowed by the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal` `my claim was allowed by the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal` `the exception applies` `the benefits were paid to me after the decision`
    WHERE
        `the exception applies` MEANS `s 114(2) subsection (1) does not apply` `the day the decision allowing my claim was given` `the day the Commission's appeal to the Appeal Division was brought` `the Commission appealed on the ground that I ought to be disentitled under section 36` `my case is one the Regulations prescribe as an exception`


§§ `Investigations, prosecutions and proof against me (ss 124 and 125)`

-- SITUATION: the Commission is investigating a matter, or has charged you with an offence under the Act. Ask "Are you being investigated
-- or charged?" before showing this group.
-- s 124(3). The public has a claim to notice of an investigation, and a person or association with an interest has a claim to be heard.
@export Must the Commission give public notice before it investigates a matter (s 124(3))?
GIVEN `the matter is one the Commission is empowered to investigate under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one that the Act empowers the Commission to investigate?
      `the Commission intends to investigate the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission intend to investigate it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commission give public notice before it investigates a matter` IF
    `s 124(3) the Commission must give public notice of its intention to investigate the matter` `the matter is one the Commission is empowered to investigate under this Act` `the Commission intends to investigate the matter`

@export Must the Commission receive my representations on a matter it is investigating (s 124(3))?
GIVEN `the matter is under investigation by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter under investigation by the Commission?
      `I appear to the Commission to have an interest in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you appear to the Commission to have an interest in the matters under investigation (the Commission's own view)?
      `I have submitted representations to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you submitted representations to the Commission?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commission receive my representations on a matter it is investigating` IF
    `s 124(3) the Commission must receive the representations` `the matter is under investigation by the Commission` `I appear to the Commission to have an interest in the matter` `I have submitted representations to the Commission`

-- s 125(2). TRUE means you are barred from objecting on that ground.
@export Am I barred from objecting that the proceeding against me relates to two or more offences (s 125(2))?
GIVEN `the proceeding is in a prosecution under this Act other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding (information, complaint, warrant, conviction or other) in a prosecution under the Act other than Part IV?
      `the proceeding relates to two or more offences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the proceeding relate to two or more offences?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from objecting that the proceeding relates to two or more offences` IF
    `s 125(2) the proceeding is not objectionable or insufficient because it relates to two or more offences` `the proceeding is in a prosecution under this Act other than Part IV` `the proceeding relates to two or more offences`

-- s 125(3). A provincial court judge may hear the case where you live, carry on business, are found, are apprehended or are in custody.
@export Can a provincial court judge hear the charge against me although the matter did not arise in the judge's jurisdiction (s 125(3))?
GIVEN `the charge is about an offence under this Act other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information or complaint about an offence under the Act other than Part IV?
      `the judge is a provincial court judge as defined in section 2 of the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge a provincial court judge as defined in section 2 of the Criminal Code?
      `I am resident within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you live within the judge's territorial jurisdiction?
      `I carry on business within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you carry on business within the judge's territorial jurisdiction?
      `I am found within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you found within the judge's territorial jurisdiction?
      `I am apprehended within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you apprehended within the judge's territorial jurisdiction?
      `I am in custody within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in custody within the judge's territorial jurisdiction?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a provincial court judge hear the charge against me although the matter did not arise in the judge's jurisdiction` IF
    `s 125(3) the judge may hear, try or determine the information or complaint although the matter did not arise within the judge's jurisdiction` `the charge is about an offence under this Act other than Part IV` `the judge is a provincial court judge as defined in section 2 of the Criminal Code` `I am resident within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` `I carry on business within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` `I am found within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` `I am apprehended within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` `I am in custody within the judge's territorial jurisdiction`

-- s 125(4). A limit on prosecution: five years after the Commission became aware of the subject-matter. For an offence under Part IV this
-- section does not speak (NOTHING).
@export Can a prosecution against me still be commenced (s 125(4))?
GIVEN `the offence is under Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence one under Part IV of the Act (premiums)?
      `the day the Commission became aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Commission become aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the day the prosecution is commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the prosecution commenced, or would it be? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a prosecution against me still be commenced` IS
    `s 125(4) a prosecution may be commenced` `the offence is under Part IV` `the day the Commission became aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution` `the day the prosecution is commenced`

@export What is the last day a prosecution against me can be commenced (s 125(4))?
GIVEN `the offence is under Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence one under Part IV of the Act (premiums)?
      `the day the Commission became aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Commission become aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day a prosecution against me can be commenced` IS
    `s 125(4) the last day on which a prosecution may be commenced` `the offence is under Part IV` `the day the Commission became aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution`

-- s 125(5). A certificate that appears to be from the Commission, certifying the day it became aware, is conclusive proof of that day.
@export Is a certificate from the Commission of the day it became aware conclusive proof against me (s 125(5))?
GIVEN `the document appears to have been issued by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document appear to have been issued by the Commission?
      `the document certifies the day the Commission became aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it certify the day on which the Commission became aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a certificate from the Commission of the day it became aware conclusive proof against me` IF
    `s 125(5) the document is admissible in evidence and is conclusive proof of the day on which the Commission became aware` `the document appears to have been issued by the Commission` `the document certifies the day the Commission became aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution`

-- s 125(6). An affidavit of a person acting for the Commission: sworn or affirmed before a commissioner of oaths or another person authorized
-- to take affidavits (s 2(1)). If it says what the section lists, it is evidence that a request, notice or demand was served on you personally.
@export Can the Commission prove by affidavit that a request, notice or demand was served on me personally (s 125(6))?
GIVEN `the affidavit was sworn or affirmed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the affidavit sworn or affirmed?
      `it was sworn or affirmed before a commissioner of oaths` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sworn or affirmed before a commissioner of oaths?
      `it was sworn or affirmed before another person authorized to take affidavits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sworn or affirmed before any other person authorized to take affidavits?
      `the person who swore it is a person acting for the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who made the affidavit a person acting for the Commission?
      `the Act or the regulations provide for personal service of this kind of request, notice or demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act (other than Part IV) or the Regulations provide for personal service of this kind of request for information, notice or demand?
      `it states that the person has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state that the person has charge of the appropriate records and knowledge of the facts in your case?
      `it states that the request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person it was directed to?
      `it identifies as an exhibit a true copy of the request, notice or demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it identify, as an exhibit attached to it, a true copy of the request, notice or demand?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission prove by affidavit that a request, notice or demand was served on me personally` IF
    `s 125(6) the affidavit is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand` `the affidavit` `the Act or the regulations provide for personal service of this kind of request, notice or demand` `it states that the person has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case` `it states that the request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed` `it identifies as an exhibit a true copy of the request, notice or demand`
    WHERE
        `the affidavit` MEANS `ei4 Affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` WITH
            `sworn or affirmed` IS `the affidavit was sworn or affirmed`
            `before a commissioner of oaths` IS `it was sworn or affirmed before a commissioner of oaths`
            `before any other person authorized to take affidavits` IS `it was sworn or affirmed before another person authorized to take affidavits`
            `the affiant is a person acting for the Commission` IS `the person who swore it is a person acting for the Commission`

-- s 125(7). An affidavit of a person acting for the Commission saying that, after a careful search of the records, no return, statement,
-- answer or certificate by you could be found, is evidence that you did not file or make it.
@export Can the Commission prove by affidavit that I did not file a return, statement, answer or certificate (s 125(7))?
GIVEN `the affidavit was sworn or affirmed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the affidavit sworn or affirmed?
      `it was sworn or affirmed before a commissioner of oaths` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sworn or affirmed before a commissioner of oaths?
      `it was sworn or affirmed before another person authorized to take affidavits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sworn or affirmed before any other person authorized to take affidavits?
      `the person who swore it is a person acting for the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who made the affidavit a person acting for the Commission?
      `I am required by the Act or the regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required by the Act (other than Part IV) or the Regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate?
      `it states that the person has charge of the appropriate records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state that the person has charge of the appropriate records?
      `it states that after a careful examination and search the person has been unable to find that the return, statement, answer or certificate was filed or made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that, after a careful examination and search of the records, the person has been unable to find that the return, statement, answer or certificate was filed or made by you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission prove by affidavit that I did not file a return, statement, answer or certificate` IF
    `s 125(7) the affidavit is evidence that in that case the person did not file or make the return, statement, answer or certificate` `the affidavit` `I am required by the Act or the regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate` `it states that the person has charge of the appropriate records` `it states that after a careful examination and search the person has been unable to find that the return, statement, answer or certificate was filed or made`
    WHERE
        `the affidavit` MEANS `ei4 Affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` WITH
            `sworn or affirmed` IS `the affidavit was sworn or affirmed`
            `before a commissioner of oaths` IS `it was sworn or affirmed before a commissioner of oaths`
            `before any other person authorized to take affidavits` IS `it was sworn or affirmed before another person authorized to take affidavits`
            `the affiant is a person acting for the Commission` IS `the person who swore it is a person acting for the Commission`

-- s 125(8). An affidavit saying that the records show your return, statement, answer or certificate was filed on a particular day is
-- evidence that it was filed on that day and not before.
@export Can the Commission prove by affidavit the day I filed a return, statement, answer or certificate (s 125(8))?
GIVEN `the affidavit was sworn or affirmed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the affidavit sworn or affirmed?
      `it was sworn or affirmed before a commissioner of oaths` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sworn or affirmed before a commissioner of oaths?
      `it was sworn or affirmed before another person authorized to take affidavits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sworn or affirmed before any other person authorized to take affidavits?
      `the person who swore it is a person acting for the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who made the affidavit a person acting for the Commission?
      `I am required by the Act or the regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required by the Act (other than Part IV) or the Regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate?
      `it states that the person has charge of the appropriate records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state that the person has charge of the appropriate records?
      `it states that after careful examination the person has found that the return, statement, answer or certificate was filed or made on a particular day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that, after careful examination of the records, the person has found that the return, statement, answer or certificate was filed or made on a particular day?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission prove by affidavit the day I filed a return, statement, answer or certificate` IF
    `s 125(8) the affidavit is evidence that the return, statement, answer or certificate was filed or made on that day and not before` `the affidavit` `I am required by the Act or the regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate` `it states that the person has charge of the appropriate records` `it states that after careful examination the person has found that the return, statement, answer or certificate was filed or made on a particular day`
    WHERE
        `the affidavit` MEANS `ei4 Affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` WITH
            `sworn or affirmed` IS `the affidavit was sworn or affirmed`
            `before a commissioner of oaths` IS `it was sworn or affirmed before a commissioner of oaths`
            `before any other person authorized to take affidavits` IS `it was sworn or affirmed before another person authorized to take affidavits`
            `the affiant is a person acting for the Commission` IS `the person who swore it is a person acting for the Commission`

-- s 125(14). In a prosecution, a return, certificate, statement or answer that appears to have been filed or delivered by you, or made or
-- signed by you, is proof that it was, unless there is evidence to the contrary.
@export Does the production of a return in court prove that I filed or signed it (s 125(14))?
GIVEN `the proceeding is a prosecution for an offence under this Act other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a prosecution for an offence under the Act other than Part IV?
      `the document is a return, certificate, statement or answer required by or under the Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a return, certificate, statement or answer required by or under the Act (other than Part IV) or the Regulations?
      `it appears to have been filed or delivered by or for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to have been filed or delivered by or for you?
      `it appears to have been made or signed by or for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to have been made or signed by or for you?
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence to the contrary?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the production of a return in court prove that I filed or signed it` IF
    `s 125(14) the production of the document is proof that it was filed or delivered by or for, or made or signed by or for, the person charged` `the proceeding is a prosecution for an offence under this Act other than Part IV` `the document is a return, certificate, statement or answer required by or under the Act or the regulations` `it appears to have been filed or delivered by or for me` `it appears to have been made or signed by or for me` `there is evidence to the contrary`

-- s 125(17). An officer, director or agent of a corporation that commits an offence is a party to it, and liable to the same punishment,
-- if they directed, authorized, assented to, acquiesced in or took part in it, whether or not the corporation is prosecuted or convicted.
@export Am I guilty of my corporation's offence as an officer, director or agent (s 125(17))?
GIVEN `my corporation commits an offence under this Act other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a corporation commit an offence under the Act other than Part IV?
      `I am an officer, director or agent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer, director or agent of the corporation?
      `I directed the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you direct the commission of the offence?
      `I authorized the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you authorize the commission of the offence?
      `I assented to the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you assent to the commission of the offence?
      `I acquiesced in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you acquiesce in the commission of the offence?
      `I participated in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you participate in the commission of the offence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of my corporation's offence as an officer, director or agent` IF
    `s 125(17) the officer, director or agent is a party to and guilty of the offence and liable on conviction to the punishment provided for it` `my corporation commits an offence under this Act other than Part IV` `I am an officer, director or agent of the corporation` `I directed the commission of the offence` `I authorized the commission of the offence` `I assented to the commission of the offence` `I acquiesced in the commission of the offence` `I participated in the commission of the offence`


§§ `Money I owe the Commission: certificates, judgments and my pay (s 126(1) to (6))`

-- SITUATION: you owe the Commission an amount under Part I, II or VII.1 and have not paid. Ask "Do you owe the Commission money that is
-- unpaid?" before showing this group.
-- s 126(1). "Certify": the Commission's formal statement of the unpaid amount, which it can then register in the Federal Court.
@export Can the Commission certify an amount I owe and have not paid (s 126(1))?
GIVEN `the Part under which I owe the amount` IS A `Part of the Act` @desc Under which Part of the Act do you owe the amount? One of: Part I, Part II, Part III, Part IV, Part V, Part VI, Part VII, Part VII.1, Part VIII, Part VIII.1, Part VIII.2, Part VIII.3, Part VIII.4, Part VIII.5, Part VIII.6, Part IX
      `I have not paid the amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount unpaid?
      `in the Commission's opinion I am attempting to avoid payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Commission's opinion, are you attempting to avoid payment?
      `the day I defaulted` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you default on the amount? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the day the Commission would certify the amount` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the Commission certify the amount? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission certify an amount I owe and have not paid` IF
    `s 126(1) the unpaid amount may be certified by the Commission` `the Part under which I owe the amount` `I have not paid the amount` `in the Commission's opinion I am attempting to avoid payment` `the day I defaulted` `the day the Commission would certify the amount`

@export From what day can the Commission certify my unpaid amount if it does not think I am avoiding payment (s 126(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the day I defaulted` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you default on the amount? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From what day can the Commission certify my unpaid amount if it does not think I am avoiding payment` IS
    `s 126(1)(b) the first day on which an unpaid amount may be certified when the person is not attempting to avoid payment` `the day I defaulted`

-- s 126(2). Once registered in the Federal Court the certificate is treated as a judgment for the amount plus interest to the day of payment.
@export How much is the Federal Court judgment against me once the Commission registers its certificate (s 126(2))?
GIVEN `the certificate has been produced to the Federal Court and registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the certificate been produced to the Federal Court and registered?
      `the amount specified in the certificate` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount does the certificate specify, in dollars?
      `the interest to the day of payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the interest to the day of payment as the Act provides (section 80.1 and its regulations), in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the Federal Court judgment against me once the Commission registers its certificate` IS
    `s 126(2) the debt for which the registered certificate has the force and effect of a judgment of the Federal Court` `the certificate has been produced to the Federal Court and registered` `the amount specified in the certificate` `the interest to the day of payment`

@export Can the costs of registering the certificate be recovered from me (s 126(3))?
GIVEN `the costs and charges are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the costs and charges reasonable?
      `the costs and charges are attendant on the registration of the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they attendant on the registration of the certificate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the costs of registering the certificate be recovered from me` IF
    `s 126(3) the costs and charges are recoverable as if they had been certified and the certificate registered` `the costs and charges are reasonable` `the costs and charges are attendant on the registration of the certificate`

-- s 126(4). "Garnishment": the Commission tells someone who owes you money to pay it to the Receiver General on account of what you owe.
-- A notice is "sent by a confirmed delivery service" when it goes by certified mail, registered mail or another service giving proof of
-- delivery (s 2(1)); one answer is asked and the core rule's other two inputs are fixed.
@export Can the Commission make someone who owes me money pay it to the Receiver General (s 126(4))?
GIVEN `the Commission knows or suspects that a person is or is about to become indebted or liable to pay me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission know or suspect that a person is, or is about to become, indebted or liable to make a payment to you?
      `I am liable to make a payment under Part I, II or VII.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you liable to make a payment under Part I, II or VII.1?
      `I am liable to make a payment under subsection 126(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you liable to make a payment under subsection 126(7) (an amount not paid as required by an earlier notice)?
      `the notice is served personally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice served personally?
      `the notice is sent by certified mail, registered mail or another delivery service that provides proof of delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice sent by certified mail, registered mail or another delivery service that provides proof of delivery?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission make someone who owes me money pay it to the Receiver General` IF
    `s 126(4) the Commission may require the first person to pay the money otherwise payable to the second person to the Receiver General on account of the second person's liability` `the Commission knows or suspects that a person is or is about to become indebted or liable to pay me` `I am liable to make a payment under Part I, II or VII.1` `I am liable to make a payment under subsection 126(7)` `the notice is served personally` `the notice is sent by a confirmed delivery service`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: only whether the notice went by one of the three means is read, so the answer feeds the third input.
        `the notice is sent by a confirmed delivery service` MEANS `s 2(1) confirmed delivery service` FALSE FALSE `the notice is sent by certified mail, registered mail or another delivery service that provides proof of delivery`

-- s 126(5)(a). If the Commission has made my employer pay part of my pay to the Receiver General, the requirement covers every later
-- payment of my pay until I have satisfied what I owe.
@export Does the Commission's requirement cover my future pay from my employer (s 126(5)(a))?
GIVEN `the Commission has required my employer to pay money otherwise payable to me as remuneration to the Receiver General on account of my liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission, by a notice under subsection 126(4), required my employer to pay to the Receiver General, on account of my liability under Part I, II or VII.1, money otherwise payable to me as remuneration?
      `the payment is a future payment of my remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment a future payment by the employer to you as remuneration?
      `my liability has been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you satisfied the liability?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Commission's requirement cover my future pay from my employer` IF
    `s 126(5)(a) the requirement is applicable to the payment` `the Commission has required my employer to pay money otherwise payable to me as remuneration to the Receiver General on account of my liability` `the payment is a future payment of my remuneration` `my liability has been satisfied`

-- s 126(6). The Commission's receipt for money my employer paid it is a good discharge of the employer's liability to me, to the extent of
-- the payment: I cannot claim from my employer the part it paid to the Receiver General. (Fork F-ei4-9 in NOTES.md.)
@export How much of what my employer owed me is discharged by its payment to the Receiver General (s 126(6))?
GIVEN `the Commission has given a receipt for money paid as required by its notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission given a receipt for money paid as required under subsection 126(4) or (5)?
      `the amount of money paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much money was paid, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of what my employer owed me is discharged by its payment to the Receiver General` IS
    `s 126(6) the amount of the original liability that the receipt discharges` `the Commission has given a receipt for money paid as required by its notice` `the amount of money paid`

@export How much of what my employer owed me can I still claim from it after its payment to the Receiver General (s 126(6))?
GIVEN `the Commission has given a receipt for money paid as required by its notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission given a receipt for money paid as required under subsection 126(4) or (5)?
      `the amount of money paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much money was paid, in dollars?
      `what my employer owed me` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did your employer owe you, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of what my employer owed me can I still claim from it` IS
    `s 126(6) the original liability that remains after the discharge` `the Commission has given a receipt for money paid as required by its notice` `the amount of money paid` `what my employer owed me`

§§ `Inspections and demands for documents (s 126(10) to (15), (21))`

-- SITUATION: an authorized person of the Commission wants to inspect your documents or premises, or the Commission has sent you a demand.
-- Ask "Has the Commission asked to inspect your records or premises, or sent you a demand for information?" before showing this group.
-- s 126(10). An "authorized person" is a person the Commission authorized in writing for the purposes of section 126 (s 126(22)).
@export Can an authorized person inspect or examine my documents (s 126(10))?
GIVEN `the person is authorized in writing by the Commission for the purposes of section 126` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person authorized in writing by the Commission for the purposes of section 126?
      `the inspection is at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the inspection at a reasonable time?
      `the inspection is for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of the Act (other than Part IV)?
      `the document relates or may relate to information that is or should be in the records or books of account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document relate, or may it relate, to the information that is or should be in the records or books of account?
      `the document relates or may relate to the amount of any benefits payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document relate, or may it relate, to the amount of any benefits payable under the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can an authorized person inspect or examine my documents` IF
    `s 126(10) an authorized person may inspect or examine the document` (`s 126(22) authorized person` `the person is authorized in writing by the Commission for the purposes of section 126`) `the inspection is at a reasonable time` `the inspection is for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `the document relates or may relate to information that is or should be in the records or books of account` `the document relates or may relate to the amount of any benefits payable`

-- s 126(10)(a) and (11). A dwelling-house may be entered only with the occupant's consent or under a warrant. "Dwelling-house" is the
-- s 2(1) definition: a residence, or a building in its yard joined to it by a doorway or covered passageway, or a mobile unit used as a residence.
@export Can an authorized person enter my premises or my home without my consent (s 126(10)(a), (11))?
GIVEN `the person is authorized in writing by the Commission for the purposes of section 126` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person authorized in writing by the Commission for the purposes of section 126?
      `the entry is for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entry for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of the Act (other than Part IV)?
      `the person believes on reasonable grounds that persons are or were employed there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the authorized person believe, on reasonable grounds, that persons are or were employed at the place?
      `the person believes on reasonable grounds that records or books of account are or should be kept there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the authorized person believe, on reasonable grounds, that records or books of account are or should be kept at the place?
      `the place is a building or structure kept or occupied as a residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place the whole or any part of a building or structure kept or occupied as your permanent or temporary residence?
      `the place is a building in the yard of my home joined to it by a doorway or covered passageway` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place a building within the yard of your home that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passageway?
      `the place is a mobile unit being used as a residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place a unit designed to be mobile and to be used as a residence that is being used as a residence?
      `I consent to the entry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, as occupant, consent to the entry?
      `the entry is under a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entry under the authority of a warrant issued by a judge?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can an authorized person enter my premises or my home without my consent` IF
    `s 126(10)(a) an authorized person may enter the premises or place` (`s 126(22) authorized person` `the person is authorized in writing by the Commission for the purposes of section 126`) `the entry is for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `the person believes on reasonable grounds that persons are or were employed there` `the person believes on reasonable grounds that records or books of account are or should be kept there` `the place is a dwelling-house` `I consent to the entry` `the entry is under a warrant`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: s 2(1) reads six facts; the doorway answer also feeds the passageway limb (which is an alternative to it) and the mobile-unit answer feeds both of its limbs.
        `the place is a dwelling-house` MEANS `s 2(1) dwelling-house` `the place is a building or structure kept or occupied as a residence` `the place is a building in the yard of my home joined to it by a doorway or covered passageway` `the place is a building in the yard of my home joined to it by a doorway or covered passageway` FALSE `the place is a mobile unit being used as a residence` `the place is a mobile unit being used as a residence`

-- s 126(10)(b). The owner, occupant or person in charge must give reasonable assistance and answer proper questions.
@export Must I give an authorized person reasonable assistance and answer proper questions at my premises (s 126(10)(b))?
GIVEN `I am the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place?
      `an authorized person is exercising the power to inspect or examine there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an authorized person inspecting or examining documents at the premises or place under subsection 126(10)?
      `the assistance is reasonable or the question is proper and relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assistance asked for reasonable, or the question asked proper and relating to the administration or enforcement of the Act (other than Part IV)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give an authorized person reasonable assistance and answer proper questions at my premises` IF
    `s 126(10)(b) the owner, occupant or person in charge must give the assistance or answer the question` `I am the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises` `an authorized person is exercising the power to inspect or examine there` `the assistance is reasonable or the question is proper and relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act`

-- s 126(12). Only a judge can issue the warrant, on the Commission's ex parte application (without notice to you), if satisfied on oath
-- on all three limbs. The satisfaction is the judge's, asked here as a conditional.
@export Can a judge issue a warrant to enter my home, if the judge is satisfied on all three points (s 126(12))?
GIVEN `the Commission has applied ex parte` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission applied to the judge ex parte (without notice to you)?
      `the person deciding is a judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person deciding a judge of a superior court with jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises, or a judge of the Federal Court?
      `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for believing that my home is a premises or place mentioned in subsection 126(10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds for believing that your home is a premises or place where persons are or were employed or records are or should be kept?
      `the judge is satisfied that entry is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied by information on oath that entry is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of the Act (other than Part IV)?
      `the judge is satisfied that entry has been refused or there are reasonable grounds for believing it will be refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied by information on oath that entry has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds for believing it will be?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a judge issue a warrant to enter my home` IF
    `s 126(12) the judge may issue a warrant authorizing an authorized person to enter the dwelling-house subject to such conditions as may be specified in the warrant` `the Commission has applied ex parte` `the person deciding is a judge` `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for believing that my home is a premises or place mentioned in subsection 126(10)` `the judge is satisfied that entry is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `the judge is satisfied that entry has been refused or there are reasonable grounds for believing it will be refused`

-- s 126(13). If the judge is not satisfied that entry is necessary, the judge may instead order the occupant to give access to documents.
@export Can a judge order me to give access to documents in my home instead (s 126(13))?
GIVEN `the judge is hearing the Commission's application for a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge hearing the Commission's application for a warrant under subsection 126(12)?
      `the judge is not satisfied that entry is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge not satisfied that entry into your home is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of the Act (other than Part IV)?
      `access has been or may be expected to be refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has access been, or may it be expected to be, refused?
      `the document is or may be expected to be kept in my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document kept, or may it be expected to be kept, in your home?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a judge order me to give access to documents in my home instead` IF
    `s 126(13) the judge may order the occupant to provide an authorized person with reasonable access to the document and make such other order as is appropriate` `the judge is hearing the Commission's application for a warrant` `the judge is not satisfied that entry is necessary` `access has been or may be expected to be refused` `the document is or may be expected to be kept in my home`

-- s 126(14), subject to (15). The Commission may require any person, by a notice served personally or sent by a confirmed delivery service,
-- to provide information or a document within a reasonable time stated in the notice.
@export Must I provide the information or document the Commission requires of me (s 126(14))?
GIVEN `the requirement is for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of the Act (other than Part IV)?
      `the notice is served on me personally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice served on you personally?
      `the notice is sent to me by certified mail, registered mail or another delivery service that provides proof of delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice sent to you by certified mail, registered mail or another delivery service that provides proof of delivery?
      `the notice states a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state a reasonable time within which to provide the information or document?
      `the requirement is for information or additional information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement for information or additional information, including an information return or supplementary return?
      `the requirement is for a document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement for a document?
      `subsection (15) bars the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection 126(15) bar the requirement (it is imposed on a third party about unnamed persons without a judge's authorization)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I provide the information or document the Commission requires of me` IF
    `s 126(14) the Commission may require the person to provide the information or document` `the requirement is for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `the notice is served on me personally` `the notice is sent by a confirmed delivery service` `the notice states a reasonable time` `the requirement is for information or additional information` `the requirement is for a document` `subsection (15) bars the requirement`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: only whether the notice went by one of the three means is read, so the answer feeds the third input.
        `the notice is sent by a confirmed delivery service` MEANS `s 2(1) confirmed delivery service` FALSE FALSE `the notice is sent to me by certified mail, registered mail or another delivery service that provides proof of delivery`

-- s 126(15). The Commission may not require a third party to give information about unnamed persons (people like me, not named) unless a
-- judge has first authorized it. TRUE means the bar applies.
@export Is the Commission barred from requiring a third party to give information about people like me without naming them (s 126(15))?
GIVEN `the requirement is imposed on a third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement imposed on a third party (someone other than the people it is about)?
      `the requirement relates to one or more unnamed persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it relate to one or more persons who are not named?
      `the Commission has first obtained a judge's authorization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission first obtained the authorization of a judge under subsection 126(16)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Commission barred from requiring a third party to give information about unnamed persons` IF
    `s 126(15) the Commission shall not impose the requirement on the third party` `the requirement is imposed on a third party` `the requirement relates to one or more unnamed persons` `the Commission has first obtained a judge's authorization`

-- s 126(21). No one may hinder, molest or interfere with, or prevent, a person doing what section 126 authorizes; and everyone must, unless
-- unable, do what section 126 requires. A failure when unable is not a contravention.
@export Have I contravened the duty of compliance in section 126 (s 126(21))?
GIVEN `I hinder, molest or interfere with a person doing what section 126 authorizes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hinder, molest or interfere with a person doing anything that section 126 authorizes?
      `I prevent or attempt to prevent a person doing what section 126 authorizes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you prevent, or attempt to prevent, a person from doing anything that section 126 authorizes?
      `I fail to do everything section 126 requires of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail to do everything that section 126 requires of you?
      `I am unable to do everything section 126 requires of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unable to do everything that section 126 requires of you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I contravened the duty of compliance in section 126` IF
    `s 126(21) the person contravenes the duty of compliance` `I hinder, molest or interfere with a person doing what section 126 authorizes` `I prevent or attempt to prevent a person doing what section 126 authorizes` `I fail to do everything section 126 requires of me` `I am unable to do everything section 126 requires of me`


§§ `What I tell the Commission, and questions that arise in court (ss 129 to 134)`

-- s 129. The Act says that giving the Commission evidence required for the proper determination of a claimant's entitlement "is an occasion
-- of qualified privilege". What that privilege covers is a matter of law outside this text, so the answer is only whether the occasion is one.
@export Is what I tell the Commission protected by qualified privilege (s 129)?
GIVEN `I give the Commission the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you giving the evidence to the Commission?
      `the evidence is written, oral or documentary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence written, oral or documentary?
      `the evidence is required for the proper determination of a claimant's entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence required for the proper determination of the entitlement of a claimant to benefits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I tell the Commission protected by qualified privilege` IF
    `s 129 the giving of the evidence is an occasion of qualified privilege` `I give the Commission the evidence` `the evidence is written, oral or documentary` `the evidence is required for the proper determination of a claimant's entitlement`

-- s 130. The Commission "may" pay in these cases; it does not have to, so the answer gives no claim to payment.
@export May the Commission pay me although someone else's failure cost me the right to claim (s 130)?
GIVEN `a person failed or neglected to comply with the Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a person (other than you) fail or neglect to comply with the Act or the Regulations?
      `because of that I lost the right to claim benefits in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Because of that failure or neglect, did you lose the right to claim, in whole or in part, benefits you would otherwise be entitled to?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission pay me although someone else's failure cost me the right to claim` IF
    `s 130 the Commission may nevertheless pay the benefits` `a person failed or neglected to comply with the Act or the regulations` `because of that I lost the right to claim benefits in whole or in part`

-- ss 131(1)(a) and (b). A question about whether employment is insurable (a question specified in section 90) that comes up in a court case
-- must be sent to an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency, and the court waits for the ruling.
@export Must the court send a question about my insurable employment to the Canada Revenue Agency and wait (s 131(1)(a))?
GIVEN `a question specified in section 90 arises in legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a question specified in section 90 (whether employment is insurable, and similar) arise in legal proceedings?
      `the question has been decided by the authorized officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the question already been decided by an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court send a question about my insurable employment to the Canada Revenue Agency and wait` IF
    `s 131(1)(a) the court must refer the question to an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency and defer further proceedings until the ruling is received` `a question specified in section 90 arises in legal proceedings` `the question has been decided by the authorized officer`

@export Must the court go on with the hearing once the Canada Revenue Agency's ruling is received (s 131(1)(b))?
GIVEN `a question specified in section 90 arose in legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a question specified in section 90 arise in the legal proceedings?
      `the court has received the ruling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court received the ruling of the authorized officer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court go on with the hearing once the Canada Revenue Agency's ruling is received` IF
    `s 131(1)(b) the court must proceed with the hearing and judgment` `a question specified in section 90 arose in legal proceedings` `the court has received the ruling`

-- s 131(2). If an appeal is made under section 91 (to the Minister of National Revenue) or section 103 (to the Tax Court of Canada), the
-- court defers judgment until that decision is received.
@export Must the court wait for the Minister of National Revenue's decision on my section 91 appeal before giving judgment (s 131(2)(a))?
GIVEN `an appeal has been made under section 91` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an appeal been made under section 91?
      `the decision of the Minister of National Revenue has been received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the decision of the Minister of National Revenue been received?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court wait for the Minister of National Revenue's decision on my appeal before giving judgment` IF
    `s 131(2)(a) the court must defer judgment until the decision of the Minister of National Revenue is received` `an appeal has been made under section 91` `the decision of the Minister of National Revenue has been received`

@export Must the court wait for the Tax Court of Canada's decision on my section 103 appeal before giving judgment (s 131(2)(b))?
GIVEN `an appeal has been made under section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an appeal been made under section 103?
      `the decision of the Tax Court of Canada has been received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the decision of the Tax Court of Canada been received?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court wait for the Tax Court of Canada's decision on my appeal before giving judgment` IF
    `s 131(2)(b) the court must defer judgment until the decision of the Tax Court of Canada is received` `an appeal has been made under section 103` `the decision of the Tax Court of Canada has been received`

-- s 132. A question the Commission could decide, arising in court, goes to the Commission first; the court waits, including for an appeal.
@export Must the court send a question the Commission could decide to the Commission and wait (s 132(1))?
GIVEN `a question that could be decided by the Commission arises in legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a question that could be decided by the Commission arise in legal proceedings?
      `the Commission's decision has been received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission's decision been received?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court send a question the Commission could decide to the Commission and wait` IF
    `s 132(1) the court must refer the question to the Commission and defer further proceedings until the Commission's decision is received` `a question that could be decided by the Commission arises in legal proceedings` `the Commission's decision has been received`

@export Must the court wait for the appeal decision if an appeal from the Commission's decision is pending (s 132(2))?
GIVEN `an appeal from a decision of the Commission is pending on the question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an appeal from a decision of the Commission, or of a person authorized by the Commission, pending on the question?
      `the appeal decision has been received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the appeal decision been received?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court wait for the appeal decision if an appeal from the Commission's decision is pending` IF
    `s 132(2) the court must defer further proceedings until the appeal decision is received` `an appeal from a decision of the Commission is pending on the question` `the appeal decision has been received`

@export Must the court go on with the hearing once it receives the decision (s 132(3))?
GIVEN `the court has received the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court received the decision?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court go on with the hearing once it receives the decision` IF
    `s 132(3) the court must proceed with the hearing and judgment` `the court has received the decision`

@export Is the decision conclusive in proceedings under the Act (s 132(3))?
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings proceedings under the Employment Insurance Act?
      `the decision is challenged in accordance with the Federal Courts Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision being challenged in accordance with the Federal Courts Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the decision conclusive in proceedings under the Act` IF
    `s 132(3) the decision is conclusive` `the proceedings are proceedings under the Act` `the decision is challenged in accordance with the Federal Courts Act`

-- s 134(2). A certificate that a notice, request, demand or other document was sent to you by mail is evidence that you received it in the
-- ordinary course of the mails.
@export Is a certificate that a notice was mailed to me evidence that I received it (s 134(2))?
GIVEN `the document appears to be a certificate of the Commission or a person authorized by it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document appear to be a certificate of the Commission or of a person authorized by the Commission?
      `the certificate says a notice, request, demand or other document was sent to me by mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the certificate to the effect that a notice, request, demand or other document was sent by mail?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a certificate that a notice was mailed to me evidence that I received it` IF
    `s 134(2) the certificate is evidence that the notice, request, demand or other document was received by the addressee in the ordinary course of the mails` `the document appears to be a certificate of the Commission or a person authorized by it` `the certificate says a notice, request, demand or other document was sent to me by mail`

§§ `Offences and punishment (ss 135 to 137)`

-- SITUATION: you are alleged to have given false information, hidden earnings, or broken the Act. Ask "Are you alleged to have broken the
-- Act or given false information?" before showing this group.
-- s 135(1). "Knowingly" and "knows" are about your state of mind; you state whether it was so.
@export Am I guilty of an offence under section 135(1)?
GIVEN `in a claim for benefits I made a representation I know to be false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In relation to a claim for benefits, did you make a representation that you know to be false or misleading?
      `being required to provide information I provided information or made a representation I know to be false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Being required under the Act or the Regulations to provide information, did you provide information or make a representation that you know to be false or misleading?
      `I knowingly failed to declare earnings for a period I claimed benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly fail to declare to the Commission all or some of your earnings for a period determined under the Regulations for which you claimed benefits?
      `I made a claim or declaration I know to be false or misleading because of non-disclosure of facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a claim or declaration that you know is false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts?
      `being the payee of a special warrant I knowingly negotiated or tried to negotiate it for benefits I am not entitled to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Being the payee of a special warrant, did you knowingly negotiate or try to negotiate it for benefits to which you are not entitled?
      `I knowingly failed to return a special warrant or an amount as section 44 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly fail to return a special warrant, or the amount or any excess amounts, as section 44 requires?
      `I imported or exported a document issued by the Commission to defraud or deceive it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you import or export, or have imported or exported, a document issued by the Commission for the purpose of defrauding or deceiving the Commission?
      `I participated in, assented to or acquiesced in an act or omission of those kinds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you participate in, assent to or acquiesce in an act or omission of any of the kinds above?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence under section 135(1)` IF
    `s 135(1) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the conduct alleged`
    WHERE
        `the conduct alleged` MEANS `ei4 Conduct alleged under section 135(1)` WITH
            `in relation to a claim for benefits, made a representation that the person knows to be false or misleading` IS `in a claim for benefits I made a representation I know to be false or misleading`
            `being required under this Act or the regulations to provide information, provided information or made a representation that the person knows to be false or misleading` IS `being required to provide information I provided information or made a representation I know to be false or misleading`
            `knowingly failed to declare to the Commission all or some of their earnings for a period determined under the regulations for which they claimed benefits` IS `I knowingly failed to declare earnings for a period I claimed benefits`
            `made a claim or declaration that the person knows is false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts` IS `I made a claim or declaration I know to be false or misleading because of non-disclosure of facts`
            `being the payee of a special warrant, knowingly negotiated or attempted to negotiate it for benefits to which the person is not entitled` IS `being the payee of a special warrant I knowingly negotiated or tried to negotiate it for benefits I am not entitled to`
            `knowingly failed to return a special warrant, or the amount or any excess amounts, as required by section 44` IS `I knowingly failed to return a special warrant or an amount as section 44 requires`
            `imported or exported a document issued by the Commission, or had it imported or exported, for the purpose of defrauding or deceiving the Commission` IS `I imported or exported a document issued by the Commission to defraud or deceive it`
            `participated in, assented to or acquiesced in an act or omission mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (f)` IS `I participated in, assented to or acquiesced in an act or omission of those kinds`

-- s 135(2). If a penalty for the offence has already been imposed under section 38, 39 or 65.1, no prosecution may be instituted.
@export Can I still be prosecuted for the offence if I was already given a penalty (s 135(2))?
GIVEN `a penalty for that offence has been imposed on me under section 38, 39 or 65.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a penalty for that offence already been imposed on you under section 38, 39 or 65.1?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still be prosecuted for the offence if I was already given a penalty` IF
    `s 135(2) a prosecution for the offence may be instituted` `a penalty for that offence has been imposed on me under section 38, 39 or 65.1`

-- s 135(3)(a). The fine is at least $200 and at most $5,000, plus (in an undeclared-earnings case) up to double the benefits cut under
-- s 19(3) and the benefits that would have been paid, or (in another case the court thinks appropriate) up to double the benefits paid
-- because of the offence. This is a cap, not an amount the court must impose.
@export What is the most I can be fined for an offence under section 135 (s 135(3)(a))?
GIVEN `my offence is a case of knowingly failing to declare earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence one of knowingly failing to declare to the Commission all or some of your earnings for a period for which you claimed benefits (paragraph 135(1)(b.1))?
      `the court thinks it an appropriate case for an addition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is not that kind of case, does the court think it an appropriate case for an addition based on the benefits paid?
      `the amount my benefits were reduced under subsection 19(3)` IS A NUMBER @desc For an undeclared-earnings case: the amount by which your benefits were reduced under subsection 19(3), in dollars (0 if not that kind of case)
      `the benefits that would have been paid for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc For an undeclared-earnings case: the benefits that would have been paid to you for the period if they had not been reduced and you had not been disentitled or disqualified, in dollars (0 if not that kind of case)
      `the benefits that may have been paid as a result of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc For another appropriate case: the benefits that may have been paid as a result of the offence, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for an offence under section 135` IS
    `s 135(3)(a) the greatest fine` `my offence is a case of knowingly failing to declare earnings` `the court thinks it an appropriate case for an addition` `the amount my benefits were reduced under subsection 19(3)` `the benefits that would have been paid for the period` `the benefits that may have been paid as a result of the offence`

-- s 135(3). The punishment is a fine of at least $200 up to the greatest fine, with or without imprisonment of up to six months.
@export Is this fine and prison term within what section 135(3) allows?
GIVEN `my offence is a case of knowingly failing to declare earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence one of knowingly failing to declare to the Commission all or some of your earnings for a period for which you claimed benefits (paragraph 135(1)(b.1))?
      `the court thinks it an appropriate case for an addition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is not that kind of case, does the court think it an appropriate case for an addition based on the benefits paid?
      `the amount my benefits were reduced under subsection 19(3)` IS A NUMBER @desc For an undeclared-earnings case: the amount by which your benefits were reduced under subsection 19(3), in dollars (0 if not that kind of case)
      `the benefits that would have been paid for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc For an undeclared-earnings case: the benefits that would have been paid to you for the period if they had not been reduced and you had not been disentitled or disqualified, in dollars (0 if not that kind of case)
      `the benefits that may have been paid as a result of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc For another appropriate case: the benefits that may have been paid as a result of the offence, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the fine` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fine, in dollars?
      `the term of imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the term of imprisonment, in months (0 if none)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this fine and prison term within what section 135(3) allows` IF
    `s 135(3) the punishment is within the limits` `the fine` `the term of imprisonment in months` `the greatest fine`
    WHERE
        `the greatest fine` MEANS `s 135(3)(a) the greatest fine` `my offence is a case of knowingly failing to declare earnings` `the court thinks it an appropriate case for an addition` `the amount my benefits were reduced under subsection 19(3)` `the benefits that would have been paid for the period` `the benefits that may have been paid as a result of the offence`

-- s 136(1). Contravening the Act or the regulations is itself an offence.
@export Am I guilty of an offence for contravening the Act or the regulations (s 136(1))?
GIVEN `I contravene the Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you contravene the Employment Insurance Act or the Regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence for contravening the Act or the regulations` IF
    `s 136(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `I contravene the Act or the regulations`

-- s 136(2). Delaying or obstructing a person authorized by the Commission in the exercise of their powers or duties is an offence.
@export Am I guilty of an offence for delaying or obstructing a person authorized by the Commission (s 136(2))?
GIVEN `I delay a person authorized by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you delay a person authorized by the Commission?
      `I obstruct a person authorized by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you obstruct a person authorized by the Commission?
      `that person is exercising their powers or performing their duties under the Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person exercising their powers or performing their duties under the Act or the Regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence for delaying or obstructing a person authorized by the Commission` IF
    `s 136(2) the person is guilty of an offence` `I delay a person authorized by the Commission` `I obstruct a person authorized by the Commission` `that person is exercising their powers or performing their duties under the Act or the regulations`

-- s 137. An offence under the Act with no penalty of its own (such as one under s 136) is punishable by a fine of $100 to $2,000, or
-- imprisonment of up to six months, or both.
@export Am I liable to the general penalty for my offence (s 137)?
GIVEN `I am guilty of an offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you guilty of an offence under the Act?
      `the Act provides a penalty for that offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act provide a penalty for that offence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable to the general penalty for my offence` IF
    `s 137 the person is liable on summary conviction to the general penalty` `I am guilty of an offence under the Act` `the Act provides a penalty for that offence`

@export Is this punishment within the general penalty (s 137)?
GIVEN `a fine is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a fine imposed?
      `the fine` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fine, in dollars (0 if none)?
      `imprisonment is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is imprisonment imposed?
      `the term of imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the term of imprisonment, in months (0 if none)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this punishment within the general penalty` IF
    `s 137 the punishment is within the limits` `a fine is imposed` `the fine` `imprisonment is imposed` `the term of imprisonment in months`

§§ `My Social Insurance Number (ss 138 and 139)`

-- s 138.
@export Must I have a Social Insurance Number (s 138)?
GIVEN `I am employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in insurable employment?
      `I am a self-employed person to whom Part VII.1 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person in respect of whom Part VII.1 applies?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I have a Social Insurance Number` IF
    `s 138 the person must have a Social Insurance Number assigned under an Act of Parliament` `I am employed in insurable employment` `I am a self-employed person to whom Part VII.1 applies`

-- s 139. A change of name (by marriage or otherwise) must be told to the Commission within 60 days, unless you already told another
-- authority empowered to receive that information.
@export Must I tell the Commission my new name after a change of name (s 139)?
GIVEN `I have a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a Social Insurance Number been assigned to you?
      `my name has changed because of marriage or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your name changed because of marriage or otherwise?
      `I have already informed another authority empowered to receive that information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already informed another authority that is empowered to receive that information?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I tell the Commission my new name after a change of name` IF
    `s 139 the person must inform the Commission of their new name` `I have a Social Insurance Number` `my name has changed because of marriage or otherwise` `I have already informed another authority empowered to receive that information`

@export By what day must I tell the Commission my new name (s 139)?
GIVEN `I have a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a Social Insurance Number been assigned to you?
      `my name has changed because of marriage or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your name changed because of marriage or otherwise?
      `I have already informed another authority empowered to receive that information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already informed another authority that is empowered to receive that information?
      `the day my change of name became effective` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the change of name become effective? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I tell the Commission my new name` IS
    `s 139 the last day on which the person must inform the Commission of their new name` `I have a Social Insurance Number` `my name has changed because of marriage or otherwise` `I have already informed another authority empowered to receive that information` `the day my change of name became effective`


§§ `Repaying benefits because my income was high (Part VII, ss 144 to 151)`

-- SITUATION: you were paid benefits in a taxation year and your income that year was high. Ask "Were you paid benefits in a year when your
-- income was high?" before showing this group.
-- s 144 "income of a person for a period": your income under the Income Tax Act, with three adjustments the Act names.
@export What is my income for the benefit repayment (s 144)?
GIVEN `my income under the Income Tax Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your income for the year under the Income Tax Act, in dollars?
      `the amount I deducted under paragraphs 60(v.1), (w), (y) and (z)` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you deduct under paragraphs 60(v.1), (w), (y) and (z) of the Income Tax Act, in dollars (0 if none)?
      `the amount included for a gain on a disposition of property to which section 79 applies` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was included in your income for a gain from a disposition of property to which section 79 of the Income Tax Act applies, in dollars (0 if none)?
      `the amount included under paragraph 56(1)(q.1) or subsection 56(6)` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was included in your income under paragraph 56(1)(q.1) or subsection 56(6) of the Income Tax Act, in dollars (0 if none)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my income for the benefit repayment` IS
    `s 144 income of a person for a period` `my income under the Income Tax Act` `the amount I deducted under paragraphs 60(v.1), (w), (y) and (z)` `the amount included for a gain on a disposition of property to which section 79 applies` `the amount included under paragraph 56(1)(q.1) or subsection 56(6)`

-- s 145(1) to (3). If your income for the year is more than 1.25 times the maximum yearly insurable earnings, you repay 30% of the lesser of
-- the benefits paid to you that year (leaving out special benefits and Part VII.1 benefits) and the amount by which your income is over
-- 1.25 times the maximum. You repay nothing if you were paid regular benefits for less than one week in the ten years before that year,
-- not counting weeks that began before 30 June 1996. No rounding.
@export How much must I repay of the benefits I was paid in the year (ss 145(1) to (3))?
GIVEN `regular benefits paid to me under Part I in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How much regular benefits (benefits because you lost your job) were paid to you under Part I in the year, in dollars?
      `regular benefits paid to me under Part VIII in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How much regular benefits were paid to you under Part VIII (self-employed fishing) in the year, in dollars?
      `special benefits paid to me under Part I in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How much special benefits (sickness, maternity, parental, caring for a family member or critically ill child or adult) were paid to you under Part I in the year, in dollars?
      `benefits paid to me under Part VII.1 in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How much benefits were paid to you under Part VII.1 (self-employed persons) in the year, in dollars?
      `my income for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your income for the year for the benefit repayment (see the question about your income), in dollars?
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year, in dollars? (a published figure; the Act gives only the formula)
      `weeks of regular benefits paid to me in the ten years before the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of regular benefits were paid to you in the ten years before the year?
      `of those weeks, the weeks that began before 30 June 1996` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those weeks, how many began before 30 June 1996?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I repay of the benefits I was paid in the year` IS
    `s 145 the benefit repayment` `my benefits` `my income for the year` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` `the weeks that count`
    WHERE
        `my benefits` MEANS LIST `my regular benefits under Part I`, `my regular benefits under Part VIII`, `my special benefits under Part I`, `my benefits under Part VII.1`
        `my regular benefits under Part I` MEANS `ei4 Benefit paid in the taxation year` WITH
            `the amount paid` IS `regular benefits paid to me under Part I in the year`
            `the Part under which the benefit is payable` IS `Part I`
            `the reason for which the benefit is paid` IS `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`
        `my regular benefits under Part VIII` MEANS `ei4 Benefit paid in the taxation year` WITH
            `the amount paid` IS `regular benefits paid to me under Part VIII in the year`
            `the Part under which the benefit is payable` IS `Part VIII`
            `the reason for which the benefit is paid` IS `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`
        -- Placeholder: only whether the reason is a special-benefit reason is read, so any one of the special reasons stands for them all.
        `my special benefits under Part I` MEANS `ei4 Benefit paid in the taxation year` WITH
            `the amount paid` IS `special benefits paid to me under Part I in the year`
            `the Part under which the benefit is payable` IS `Part I`
            `the reason for which the benefit is paid` IS `pregnancy`
        -- Placeholder: Part VII.1 pays only special benefits (s 152.14(1)), and the Part alone excludes it.
        `my benefits under Part VII.1` MEANS `ei4 Benefit paid in the taxation year` WITH
            `the amount paid` IS `benefits paid to me under Part VII.1 in the year`
            `the Part under which the benefit is payable` IS `Part VII.1`
            `the reason for which the benefit is paid` IS `pregnancy`
        `the weeks that count` MEANS `s 145(3) the weeks of regular benefits taken into account when applying subsection (2)` `weeks of regular benefits paid to me in the ten years before the year` `of those weeks, the weeks that began before 30 June 1996`

@export Am I excused from the repayment because I was paid regular benefits for less than one week in the ten years before (s 145(2))?
GIVEN `weeks of regular benefits paid to me in the ten years before the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of regular benefits were paid to you in the ten years before the year?
      `of those weeks, the weeks that began before 30 June 1996` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those weeks, how many began before 30 June 1996?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I excused from the repayment because I was paid regular benefits for less than one week in the ten years before` IF
    `s 145(2) subsection (1) does not apply because the claimant was paid regular benefits for less than one week in the ten years before the taxation year` `the weeks that count`
    WHERE
        `the weeks that count` MEANS `s 145(3) the weeks of regular benefits taken into account when applying subsection (2)` `weeks of regular benefits paid to me in the ten years before the year` `of those weeks, the weeks that began before 30 June 1996`

-- s 145(4). The repayment is due by April 30 of the next year, or within six months of death if the claimant dies after October and
-- before May. The questions are asked of the claimant (or the person acting for the estate).
@export By what day must I make the repayment (s 145(4))?
GIVEN `the taxation year` IS A NUMBER @desc For which taxation year is the repayment (for example 2025)?
      `the claimant has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the claimant died?
      `the day of the claimant's death` IS A DATE @desc If the claimant has died, on what day? (YYYY-MM-DD). If not, give any date: it is ignored.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I make the repayment` IS
    `s 145(4) the last day on which the repayment must be made` `the taxation year` `the death, if any`
    WHERE
        `the death, if any` MEANS IF `the claimant has died` THEN JUST `the day of the claimant's death` ELSE NOTHING

@export Does a repayment I make reduce the weeks of regular benefits counted for the ten-year exception (s 145(5))?
GIVEN `this is a repayment under section 145` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a repayment under section 145?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a repayment I make reduce the weeks of regular benefits counted for the ten-year exception` IS
    `s 145(5) the repayment affects the determination under subsection (2) of regular benefits paid` `this is a repayment under section 145`

-- s 146. A return has to be filed with the Minister (of National Revenue) as part of the income tax return, when a repayment is due.
@export Must I file a benefit repayment return (s 146)?
GIVEN `my benefit repayment for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your benefit repayment for the year, in dollars (see the question about the repayment)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I file a benefit repayment return` IF
    `s 146 the claimant is required to make a benefit repayment for the taxation year` `my benefit repayment for the year`

@export By what day must the benefit repayment return be filed (s 146)?
GIVEN `the taxation year` IS A NUMBER @desc For which taxation year is the return (for example 2025)?
      `the claimant has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the claimant died?
      `the day of the claimant's death` IS A DATE @desc If the claimant has died, on what day? (YYYY-MM-DD). If not, give any date: it is ignored.
      `my filing-due date for the year under the Income Tax Act` IS A DATE @desc What is your filing-due date for the year as the Income Tax Act defines it? (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the Minister has given written notice naming a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister of National Revenue, by notice in writing, required a person to file the return within a time the notice specifies?
      `the day the Minister's notice specifies` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the notice specifies (YYYY-MM-DD). If not, give any date: it is ignored.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the benefit repayment return be filed` IS
    `s 146 the last day on which the return must be filed` `the taxation year` `the death, if any` `my filing-due date for the year under the Income Tax Act` `the notice day, if any`
    WHERE
        `the death, if any` MEANS IF `the claimant has died` THEN JUST `the day of the claimant's death` ELSE NOTHING
        `the notice day, if any` MEANS IF `the Minister has given written notice naming a day` THEN JUST `the day the Minister's notice specifies` ELSE NOTHING

@export Who must file the benefit repayment return (s 146)?
GIVEN `the claimant died after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the claimant die after October 31 in the taxation year and before May 1 in the next year?
      `the claimant is unable to file the return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claimant, for any reason, unable to file the return?
      `the Minister has required a person by written notice to file because the return was not filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the claimant or their legal representative not filed the return, and has the Minister required a person by notice in writing to file it?
GIVETH A `ei4 Who must file the return`
DECIDE `Who must file the benefit repayment return` IS
    `s 146 who must file the return` `the claimant died after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year` `the claimant is unable to file the return` `the Minister has required a person by written notice to file because the return was not filed`

-- s 147.
@export Must my return include my estimate of the benefit repayment (s 147)?
GIVEN `I am a claimant or other person required by section 146 to file a return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a claimant or other person required by section 146 to file a return?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my return include my estimate of the benefit repayment` IF
    `s 147 the return must contain the person's estimate of the benefit repayment payable` `I am a claimant or other person required by section 146 to file a return`

-- s 148 with s 144 "Minister". No fact is asked: the Act names the Minister of National Revenue.
@export Who administers and enforces the benefit repayment (s 148)?
GIVETH A Party
DECIDE `Who administers and enforces the benefit repayment` IS
    `s 148 the office that administers and enforces this Part`

-- s 150. A benefit repayment, interest, a penalty or another amount payable by a claimant under Part VII, or under the Income Tax Act
-- provisions that s 149 applies to it, is a debt due to Her Majesty.
@export Is what I owe under Part VII a debt due to the Crown (s 150)?
GIVEN `it is a benefit repayment, interest, penalty or other amount payable by me under Part VII` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount a benefit repayment, interest, a penalty or another amount payable by you under Part VII?
      `it is payable by me under an Income Tax Act provision applied to Part VII` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount payable by you under a provision of the Income Tax Act as it applies for the purposes of Part VII (section 149)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I owe under Part VII a debt due to the Crown` IF
    `s 150 the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty` `it is a benefit repayment, interest, penalty or other amount payable by me under Part VII` `it is payable by me under an Income Tax Act provision applied to Part VII`

@export Where can the Crown recover what I owe under Part VII (s 150)?
GIVEN `it is a benefit repayment, interest, penalty or other amount payable by me under Part VII` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount a benefit repayment, interest, a penalty or another amount payable by you under Part VII?
      `it is payable by me under an Income Tax Act provision applied to Part VII` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount payable by you under a provision of the Income Tax Act as it applies for the purposes of Part VII (section 149)?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `ei4 Way a debt due Her Majesty is recoverable`)
DECIDE `Where can the Crown recover what I owe under Part VII` IS
    `s 150 the ways in which the debt due to Her Majesty is recoverable` `it is a benefit repayment, interest, penalty or other amount payable by me under Part VII` `it is payable by me under an Income Tax Act provision applied to Part VII`

-- s 151(1). The Minister of National Revenue may give the Commission (or a person it authorizes) your tax information that is necessary to
-- administer and enforce Part VII or section 43 of the Act.
@export May the tax authority give my tax information to the Commission (s 151(1))?
GIVEN `the information was obtained under the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information obtained under the Income Tax Act?
      `it is necessary for the administration and enforcement of Part VII` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it necessary for the administration and enforcement of Part VII?
      `it is necessary for the administration and enforcement of section 43` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it necessary for the administration and enforcement of section 43 of the Act?
      `it is communicated to the Commission or a person it authorizes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it communicated to the Commission, or to a person authorized by the Commission?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the tax authority give my tax information to the Commission` IF
    `s 151(1) the Minister may communicate, or allow to be communicated, the information` `the information was obtained under the Income Tax Act` `it is necessary for the administration and enforcement of Part VII` `it is necessary for the administration and enforcement of section 43` `it is communicated to the Commission or a person it authorizes`

-- s 151(2). A person the Commission authorizes is treated as an official under the Income Tax Act and is bound by its confidentiality rules.
@export Is a person the Commission authorizes bound by the Income Tax Act's confidentiality rules for my information (s 151(2))?
GIVEN `the information was obtained under section 151(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information obtained under subsection 151(1)?
      `the person is authorized by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a person authorized by the Commission?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a person the Commission authorizes bound by the Income Tax Act's confidentiality rules for my information` IF
    `s 151(2) the person is an official or authorized person within the meaning of subsection 241(10) of the Income Tax Act and is subject to subsections 239(2.2) and 241(1) and (2) of that Act` `the information was obtained under section 151(1)` `the person is authorized by the Commission`

§§ `The alternate-access scheme and interim orders (Parts VIII.1 and VIII.3)`

-- SITUATION: you have worked at least 600 hours but do not qualify for benefits under section 7, or an interim order made in 2020 is said
-- to affect you. Ask "Do you have 600 or more hours of insurable employment but not enough to qualify under section 7?" before showing this.
-- s 153.1(1) and (3). The alternate-access scheme is for insured persons with at least 600 hours who do not qualify under section 7, and may
-- not give special benefits to a person subject to a section 7.1 increase in the hours required.
@export Is the alternate-access scheme meant to give me special benefits (s 153.1)?
GIVEN `I am an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an insured person (employed, or formerly employed, in insurable employment)?
      `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period?
      `I qualify to receive benefits under section 7` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify to receive benefits under section 7?
      `I am subject to an increase under section 7.1 in the hours I need` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to an increase under section 7.1 in the number of hours of insurable employment required to qualify for benefits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the alternate-access scheme meant to give me special benefits` IF
    `s 153.1 the scheme is meant to give the person special benefits` `I am an insured person` `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` `I qualify to receive benefits under section 7` `I am subject to an increase under section 7.1 in the hours I need`

-- s 153.3(1) to (4) and (9). An interim order could be made only to mitigate the economic effects of COVID-19, not in respect of Part IV or VII
-- (so not the benefit repayment), with the consent of the Minister of Finance (and, for Part III, the President of the Treasury Board too),
-- and not after 30 September 2020.
@export Was an interim order that changed my rights validly made (s 153.3)?
GIVEN `the order was made to mitigate the economic effects of COVID-19` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the order made for the purpose of mitigating the economic effects of the coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19)?
      `the order adds, adapts or disapplies provisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order add provisions, adapt provisions, or provide that provisions do not apply?
      `the order is in respect of Part IV or VII` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order in respect of Part IV or Part VII?
      `the order is in respect of a regulation for Part IV or VII` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order in respect of a regulation made under the Act for the purposes of Part IV or VII?
      `the Minister of Finance consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister of Finance consent?
      `the order is in respect of Part III or a regulation for Part III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order in respect of Part III, or of a regulation made under the Act for the purposes of that Part?
      `the President of the Treasury Board additionally consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the President of the Treasury Board additionally consent?
      `the day the order was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the order made? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was an interim order that changed my rights validly made` IF
    `s 153.3 an interim order may be made` `the order was made to mitigate the economic effects of COVID-19` `the order adds, adapts or disapplies provisions` `the order is in respect of Part IV or VII` `the order is in respect of a regulation for Part IV or VII` `the Minister of Finance consented` `the order is in respect of Part III or a regulation for Part III` `the President of the Treasury Board additionally consented` `the day the order was made`

@export Can an interim order apply to me retroactively (s 153.3(6))?
GIVEN `the interim order provides that it has retroactive effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the interim order provide that it has retroactive effect?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can an interim order apply to me retroactively` IF
    `s 153.3(6) the interim order has retroactive effect` `the interim order provides that it has retroactive effect`

-- s 153.3(7). The added provisions, adaptations and disapplications stop applying on the earliest of: the day the order specifies, the day it is
-- repealed, and the Saturday after the first anniversary of the day it takes effect.
@export On what day does an interim order's change stop applying to me (s 153.3(7))?
GIVEN `the order specifies a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the interim order specify a day on which its provisions cease to apply?
      `the day the order specifies` IS A DATE @desc If so, that day (YYYY-MM-DD). If not, give any date: it is ignored.
      `the order has been repealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the interim order been repealed?
      `the day the order was repealed` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day (YYYY-MM-DD)? If not, give any date: it is ignored.
      `the day the order takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the interim order take effect? (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does an interim order's change stop applying to me` IS
    `s 153.3(7) the day on which the added provisions, adaptations and non-application provisions must cease to apply` `the specified day, if any` `the repeal day, if any` `the day the order takes effect`
    WHERE
        `the specified day, if any` MEANS IF `the order specifies a day` THEN JUST `the day the order specifies` ELSE NOTHING
        `the repeal day, if any` MEANS IF `the order has been repealed` THEN JUST `the day the order was repealed` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 153.3(8). An order that says it applies despite the Act prevails over the Act or a regulation to the extent of a conflict.
@export Does an interim order prevail over the Act where they conflict (s 153.3(8))?
GIVEN `the order says it applies despite any provision of the Act or a regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the interim order or added provision say that it applies despite any provision of the Act or of a regulation made under it?
      `the order conflicts with the Act or a regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it conflict with the Act or a regulation made under it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does an interim order prevail over the Act where they conflict` IF
    `s 153.3(8) the interim order or added provision prevails to the extent that it conflicts with this Act or a regulation` `the order says it applies despite any provision of the Act or a regulation` `the order conflicts with the Act or a regulation`
